{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 18,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Expressions Using Letter-Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.088,
            0.723,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "• the number to the right of ‘a’ will be **1 more than it**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.113,
            0.648,
            0.131
          ],
          "content": "the number below ‘a’ will be **7 more than it**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.136,
            0.696,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": "• the number diagonal to ‘a’ will be **8 more than it**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.161,
            0.695,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": "So the other numbers in the 2 × 2 square can be represented as shown in the grid. Let us find the diagonal sums; $a \\pm ( a \\pm 8 )$ , and $(a + 1) + (a + 7)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.217,
            0.389,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "Let us simplify them."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.706,
            0.148,
            0.843,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": "| a | a + 1 |\n| --- | --- |\n| a + 7 | a + 8 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_table_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.235,
            0.695,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "Since the terms can be added in any order, the brackets can be opened."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.272,
            0.461,
            0.288
          ],
          "content": "a + (a + 8) = a + a + 8 = 2a + 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.29,
            0.68,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "(a + 1) + (a + 7) = a + 1 + a + 7 = a + a + 1 + 7 = 2a + 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.308,
            0.848,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": "We see that both diagonal sums are equal to $2 a \\: + \\: 8$ (8 more than 2 times a)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.354,
            0.847,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "Verify this expression for diagonal sums by considering any $2 \\times 2$ square and taking its top left number to be ‘a’."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.404,
            0.848,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "Thus, we have shown that diagonal sums are equal for any value of a, i.e., for any 2 × 2 square!"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.455,
            0.232,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.459,
            0.825,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": "This problem is an example that shows the power of algebraic modelling in verifying whether a pattern will always hold."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.514,
            0.846,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "Consider a set of numbers from the calendar (having endless rows) forming under the following shape:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.571,
            0.376,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.396,
            0.558,
            0.602,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": "|  | 8 |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 14 | 15 | 16 |\n|  | 22 |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_table_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.689,
            0.847,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": "? Find the sum of all the numbers. Compare it with the number in the centre: 15. Repeat this for another set of numbers that forms this shape. What do you observe?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.757,
            0.832,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "We see that the total sum is always 5 times the number in the centre."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.785,
            0.637,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "Will this always happen? How do you show this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.772,
            0.905,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.817,
            0.846,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "[**Hint:** Consider a general set of numbers that forms this shape. Take the number at the centre to be ‘a’. Express the other numbers in terms of ‘a’.] 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.872,
            0.802,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": "Find other shapes for which the sum of the numbers within the figure is always a multiple of one of the numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.858,
            0.905,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": "Math Talk"
        },
